    "Visa application procedure | Univerzita Pardubice\nSkip to main content\nVisa application procedure\nVISA APPLICATION PROCEDURE\nIf you need to apply for a visa to enter the Czech Republic, we recommend that you obtain the specific requirements directly from the Czech Embassy/Consulate in your home country.\nPlease note that the visa procedure takes 60 days, so make sure you arrange your appointment at the Embassy on time to start the semester on time.\nAfter submitting your application as well as all required documents, our International office will send you the documents you need for your visa application, as:\n1. Confirmation of Acceptance\n(Potvrzení o přijetí ke studiu – in Czech)\n2. Proof of Accommodation\n(Smlouva o smlouvě budoucí – in Czech; the English version for your information is below)\nto be able to issue these documents, we need you to pay the deposit for accommodation at the Dormitory office as soon as possible,\nYou will get all the necessary information concerning the bank account data by email from the dormitory administrator,\nFor further enquiries regarding accommodation, please contact\nubytovani@upce.cz\nThe above-mentioned documents will be sent to the International Office of your home university by regular post; therefore, it is very important to provide us with the correct postal address of your university. You can also arrange for an express delivery service (such as DHL, FedEx, or Cargo) to pick up the letter from our office. This service will be at your own expense.\nAs the visa procedure takes 60 days, we recommend you to upload all required documents into the Portal account as soon as possible to get the visa documents on time. You are also asked to arrange your appointment at the Embassy as soon as possible (July is recommended for the winter semester; November for the summer semester).\nYou can get more information about the visa application procedure at the Czech Embassies or Consulates in your home country. You may get the contact details from the website of the\nMinistry of Foreign Affairs of the Czech Republic\n.\nFast track\nIt is a tool that helps to accelerate the procedure of visa/long-term permit application.\nWho is eligible?\nThe students of the third countries (excluding EU countries, Iceland, Liechtenstein, Norway, and Switzerland), who are accepted to study in the Czech Republic based on bilateral or multilateral international agreements and governmental resolution. The project includes Erasmus+ students (International credit mobility, also known as Erasmus+ KA171) and the Fulbright programme.\nHow does it work?\nThe students are nominated by the host institution. The University informs the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, which forwards the information to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the relevant Embassy. The embassy arranges an appointment with the student within 14 days. The embassy sends the application to the Ministry of the Interior (OAMP) within 7 days. The Ministry of the Interior makes a decision within 30 days, and the embassy invites the student to collect the visa.\nHow much does it cost?\nThe fee for a long-term visa is 2500 CZK. The embassy can waive the fee in this case (a visa for the purpose of study).\nWhat do I have to do?\nIn case you are interested in being included in the Fast Track procedure, please contact your host institution coordinator,\nMartina Votoupalová\n(\nmartina.votoupalova@upce.cz\n). She might ask you to provide your personal data, such as your passport number or telephone number, if it is not available in your Portal account. At the same time, gather your documents for the visa application so that you are ready for the appointment at the Embassy.\nForms\nFiles for download\nSize\nProof of Accommodation_template - pdf\n193 kB\nUniversity of Pardubice\nMap\nContacts\n​\nContacts\nFaculties and Central Services and Facilites\nPanoramic view\nExchange/Erasmus+\nInternational students\nMagazine MY UPCE\nWebsite feedback\nServices\nAccommodation\nLibrary\nDepartment of Physical Education and Sports\nNostrification\nE-shop\nThe Centre for Technology  and Knowledge Transfer\nLanguage Centre\nGuidebook for Internationals\nEuropean University Alliance\n© 2023\nUniversity of Pardubice\n,\nStudentská 95\n,\n532 10\nPardubice 2\nPhone:\n+420 466 036 111, 466 036 112, 466 036 113\nWebmaster\n,\nRSS\nData box ID:\nf5vj9hu\nAccessibility Statement\nCC BY-NC-ND 4.0"
